---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../../styles/explorer.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Player Explorer · The Multi Sport Scouter"
  description="Explore curated athlete profiles, native role ratings, next-season estimates, and transparent cross-sport role analogies."
>
  <section class="explorer-hero shell">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Multi Sport Scouting</p>
      <h1>The Player Explorer</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="explorer-hero-copy">
      <p><strong>How to read this explorer</strong>: The first model infer how well a player performs in their native sport and role compared to their peers. These results then anchor every experimental comparison shown later.</p>
      <p><strong>Important:</strong> Cross-sport scores describe how a player's profile may fit another sport. It is not the probability of a successful transition.</p>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="reading-order shell" aria-label="How to read the profile">

    <div><span>1</span><strong>Native Sport Analysis</strong><small>How does a player actually perform in their own sport?</small></div>
    <div><span>2</span><strong>Next Season Performance Validation</strong><small>Can we reliably forecast player perform in future seasons? <br>(validation performed on 2025 data)</small></div>
    <div><span>3</span><strong>Cross-Sport Role Comparision</strong><small>How might a players archetype translate to other sports?</small></div>
  </section>

  <section class="explorer shell" aria-labelledby="explorer-title">
    <div class="explorer-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Curated portfolio edition</p>
        <h2 id="explorer-title">Player profile</h2>
      </div>
      <p id="snapshot-note">Loading the saved player list…</p>
    </div>

    <div id="app-error" class="notice error" role="alert" hidden></div>
    <div id="explorer-grid" class="explorer-grid" aria-busy="true">
      <aside class="player-picker panel" aria-label="Choose an athlete">
        <div class="picker-controls">
          <label for="player-search">Search the featured athletes</label>
          <input id="player-search" type="search" placeholder="Name, team, or position" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" />
          <label for="source-sport">Their current league</label>
          <select id="source-sport">
            <option value="all">All four leagues</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <p class="player-count"><strong id="player-count">—</strong> athletes match</p>
        <div id="player-list" class="player-list" aria-label="Athletes">
          <p class="empty-state">Loading athletes…</p>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <article id="result" class="result" aria-busy="true">
        <div class="loading panel"><span aria-hidden="true"></span><p>Building the player profile…</p></div>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p id="announcement" class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  </section>

  <section class="reading-guide shell">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Reading the numbers</p>
      <h2>One profile, three different questions.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="guide-grid">
      <p><strong>Observed home-role score</strong>Where did this player rank against peers in the same role and season?</p>
      <p><strong>Native forecast</strong>What does the experimental model estimate for the following season in that same role?</p>
      <p><strong>Cross-sport fit</strong>How does the athlete’s build—or build plus broad playing profile—resemble another role?</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <script src="../../scripts/explorer.js"></script>
</BaseLayout>

